<!--
    No-return names from public declarations (`noreturn_known`).

    Issue: the vendored no-return lists lacked functions that public headers
    and sources declare never to return, so a call to one kept a fall-through
    into whatever followed it: glibc `_Exit` and `thrd_exit`, libstdc++
    `std::rethrow_exception`, and every Rust panic helper under v0 mangling,
    the default of current rustc, whose `_RNv...` symbols the legacy
    `_ZN...17h` prefixes in the Rust list never match.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement (`kuna-analysis`
    `loader/noreturn.rs` and the lists under `kuna-analysis/data/`).

    P0 assertion: `option noreturn_known on|off` (with `noreturn_extern` and
    `noreturn_externmatch` off in the first pass, which read the same ELF list
    at flow time).

    Fixtures: `noreturn_names_x86_64` (g++ -O2, source
    `noreturn_names_x86_64.cc`) and `rust_noreturn_v0_x86_64` (rustc 1.98.1
    -C opt-level=2 -C overflow-checks=on, a `no_std` image, source
    `rust_noreturn_v0_x86_64.rs`).

    A last pair loads `rust_noreturn_pie_x86_64`, the same source linked as a
    PIE, whose calls reach the panic helpers through `R_X86_64_RELATIVE` `.got`
    slots: with `relronoreturn` off `ActionDeindirect` binds them and restarts the
    function to plant the halt, with it on the halt is planted during flow and
    nothing restarts; both read the same.

    Pass 1 (both options off) is the BUG: no call is marked no-return, the C++
    functions are truncated at the next entry and the Rust ones run into their
    int3 padding. Pass 2 (default) is the FIX: every listed call is no-return.
-->
